[results]
The paper reports that DNA damage treatment generated many p53-bound sites and that p53 directly regulates a set of target genes, including autophagy genes. p53 induced autophagy in a transactivation-dependent manner. Autophagy deficiency did not compromise DNA damage-induced cell cycle arrest or survival, but it impaired p53-dependent apoptosis and compromised transformation suppression. The provided excerpt does not include numeric fold changes, p-values, effect sizes, or sample sizes, so quantitative outcomes are not available.
